OK.  Berserker rage is +X to melee damage, +X to hit, +X to current/max 
HP, and -X to AC while in effect, never worse than AC 10.  Can't cast 
spells (too pissed).  -X to hit with thrown/fired weapons, but still +X 
to damage (can't aim, too pissed, but boy you throw hard).  Can read 
scrolls but with a chance they'll react as though confused.  No movement 
restrictions or "the computer moving for you", because those are 
instakills in too many situations.  No dropping your armor or your 
weapon -- possibly unwielding your weapon and going bare-handed though 
(note the big difference, as you don't lose the weapon).

Melee-oriented classes (Valk, Barb, Cave at the top) and brutish or 
brawly races (orc, dwarf) should be noticeably more subject to this, 
because obviously no spells is a major hazard for an Elven Wizard. 
Possibly base the chances of it happening on current INT/WIS.  I'm not 
sure what the best form of inflicting this on the player might be, 
although certainly there should be a good chance that being insulted by 
an imp, etc. might trigger it.  I'm thinking it needs to be a magic-type 
effect of some sort, and possibly a potion as well, but that will take a 
lot of pondering as to where it can fit in.

Want me to continue?  That took five minutes, and it already covers most 
of the holes you left -- AND adds something to the game noticeably, 
because +X dam/+X hit/+X HP is always something nice to have, especially 
when you've got, oh, i dunno, a cloak of displacement or an already-high 
AC.  Low-level players are already often AC-hosed, so this would 
actually be a benefit.  It'll be a lot easier to add deleterious effects 
(such as a bigger AC penalty) once the whole thing is fleshed out.

